\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we normalize masked pretraining loss}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}

\p{The autoregressive token loss follows
\citet{Section 7}{phuong2022formal}. Kaplan et al. report language-model loss
with parameter and compute variables in
\citet{sec. 2.1}{kaplan2020scaling}. We formulate the population
ratio-of-expectations and finite per-token ratio in \ref{ftip-001C} and
\ref{ftip-001E} to expose the prediction mask and normalization. Neither cited
source defines those exact ratios.}

\p{A theorem or experiment using another record weighting, length weighting,
or expectation order must state that change rather than reuse these symbols.}
